# Canonical cross-platform line-ending policy: the repository stores LF
# only; .gitattributes (not per-developer core.autocrlf) is the single
# source of truth. Modern Windows tooling (Visual Studio, VS Code, dotnet
# CLI, Go, PowerShell) handles LF working trees fine.

# Auto-detect text files, normalize to LF in the repo and working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts genuinely require CRLF (cmd.exe label parsing).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries — never normalize or diff.
*.snk binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
